@@ -0,0 +1,65 @@
+# Automatic Fastboot return — reset-side feasibility audit
+
+Date: 2026-11-20 (Asia/Shanghai). Scope: host-only assessment. **No implementation, production edit, phone query, USB open, boot/Fastboot/ADB/QEMU command, or Git mutation.** All new files are within `evidence/fastboot-return-audit-20261120/reset/`. Main owns the combined report and kernel/loader integration.
+
+## Decision
+
+**Possible in principle; medium-high overall difficulty; currently unverified. Passing `bootloader` to the existing `ResetSystem` does not implement Fastboot return.** The easy portion is specifying an opt-in terminal action. The larger work is preserving explicit normal/drained eligibility and implementing a board-supported reset-reason/PMIC/secure-reset contract with a safe diagnostic fallback.
+
+Do **not** claim warm reset is required. The examined stock lithium DT bundle enables `qcom,store-hard-reset-reason`; under that property and with download mode off, the pinned MiCode code chooses **PMIC hard reset**, stores a PMIC bootloader reason, and also writes IMEM. Whether current PSCI alone could preserve and deliver an explicitly prepared reason is **unverified**.
+
+## Current port: string ignored, warm equals cold
+
+- `ports/hakios-lithium/firmware/lithiumPkg/Library/ResetSystemLib/ResetSystem.c:6–18`: `Psci` zeroes arguments and sets only the function ID; `ResetCold` calls `0x84000009`; `ResetWarm` and `ResetPlatformSpecific` call `ResetCold`. `ResetSystem` handles shutdown specially and otherwise calls `ResetCold`, ignoring status/size/data. SHA256 **53c6ee09a80e3a1c364cafcac9ab9a8da501aff5efd38ea5975c049403d8a08e**.
+- `ResetSystemLib.inf:4–16` binds `HwResetSystemLib` and lists only `ArmSmcLib` / `BaseMemoryLib`. `lithium.dsc:54,66–69` selects it with ResetSystemRuntimeDxe. No command parser or PMIC reason programming exists in this reset implementation.
+- `Library/MemoryMapLib/MemoryMap.c:12–33` does not declare an IMEM region. Adding a write to the current port requires an explicit valid mapping/access contract, not only a numeric address.
+
+## Concrete stock lithium address evidence
+
+Read-only parsed the local official package `lithium_images_V9.5.2.0.NAHCNFA_20180405.0000.00_7.0_cn/images/boot.img`; SHA256 **2c070c67b07000a02de42fa05a6bcd93b7c32b3770d3fa9e495f321626278f44**. No binary was copied or emitted. `stock-dt-evidence.json` records 20 structurally parsed embedded DTB candidates, their offsets, lengths, SHA256s and selected reset metadata. Their examined reset metadata has **one** variant:
+
+- `/soc/qcom,msm-imem@66bf000`: `ranges = <0 0x066bf000 0x1000>`; child `restart_reason@65c`: `reg = <0x65c 4>`. Derived physical location: **0x066bf65c**.
+- `/soc/restart@4ab000`: PS_HOLD register `0x004ab000`, plus TCSR boot-misc-detect `0x007b3000`.
+- Main `qcom,pm8994@0/qcom,power-on@800`: `qcom,system-reset` and **`qcom,store-hard-reset-reason` present**. Secondary PON reset is declared and its hard-reset poweroff type is `0x4`.
+
+Example: first DTB is at boot-image offset **0xb9f4bf**, length **446650**, SHA256 **00ee2a82c28746d038caf06610a57a992c0b55f02258d92e058c3942d6aa6155**. These are stock-package metadata, not a live-selected DT or installed device-build measurement. All 20 candidates agreeing strengthens the packaged-board evidence but does not establish runtime access or reset retention. **0x77665500 is a written command VALUE, never the target physical address.**
+
+## Pinned primary producer source: IMEM + PMIC, conditional reset type
+
+MiCode/Xiaomi_Kernel_OpenSource commit **1492c8e4373b7428bb0accc4f4881e97b36508b9**, original acquisition reference `scorpio-n-oss`. The R31 acquisition's exact commit/root-tree evidence is reused. Every newly obtained file was checked by canonical Git blob SHA1 against that complete pinned tree. This is general MSM8996/Xiaomi producer evidence; it is **not lithium aboot consumer source**.
+
+1. `drivers/power/reset/msm-poweroff.c:293–307`: if `qpnp_pon_check_hard_reset_stored()` is true, only download mode sets `need_warm_reset`; otherwise a nonempty command also requests warm reset. Therefore with the stock property true and dload false, `bootloader` uses **PON_POWER_OFF_HARD_RESET**, not warm. Lines **315–318** program `PON_RESTART_REASON_BOOTLOADER` and write `0x77665500` to mapped `restart_reason`. Lines **573–587** derive mappings through DT. SHA256 **5d8b9c61b7fa4a6b6fe4832a51ced81d74771ef993c8336010886c4fc34491fc**.
+2. `drivers/platform/msm/qpnp-power-on.c:355–390,2408–2411`: the DT property controls `store_hard_reset_reason`. PMIC restart reason uses a masked SPMI write of `(reason << 2)` to `PON_SOFT_RB_SPARE` bits 7:2; no PMIC or disabled property returns success without storage. The register macro is `base + 0x8f` at line **99**. `include/linux/qpnp/power-on.h:54–63` defines BOOTLOADER **2**. Do not treat this PMIC register offset as a CPU physical address. SHA256 **bca15aaab14c0d489ca624d154dee313a4ad20bd2b0ea68f069d692d490f8c3e**.
+3. `qpnp-power-on.c:460–520,534–575`: main and possible secondary PMIC reset configuration, reset-enable sequencing and a 500us delay are part of this implementation; it is not one IMEM store. Register access is SPMI masked read/modify/write at **307–328**. The stock secondary override matters if reproducing the hard-reset branch.
+4. `msm-poweroff.c:357–362,373–410`: cache flushing and terminal SCM/PS_HOLD path, SDI and PMIC-arbiter handling are distinct from current PSCI. `arch/arm64/kernel/psci.c:268–275` invokes generic SYSTEM_RESET with zero arguments; source at **382** registers that generic callback, whereas the MSM driver installs `do_msm_restart` at **601**. Generic PSCI text does not establish the installed secure firmware's underlying mechanism or retention.
+5. `arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/msm8996.dtsi:1826–1846` independently corroborates the IMEM base/offset; **300–305** declares PS_HOLD/TCSR. SHA256 **d396978f4706a63576e51fb8df0dc1e10d8254c169ded988987b6dcc42eb6578**.
+
+Immutable primary URLs, exact file hashes, computed/tree Git blobs and reviewed line ranges are in `acquired-sources.json` and `source-manifest.json`; the public text copies are adjacent. No full clone was made.
+
+## Existing lithium reset code / bootloader boundary
+
+The local `upstream/research/edk2-lithium` checkout HEAD is **8cb11dff6e3ce5e491297188179aa7327f07a8cf**. `XiaomiMIXPkg/CommonDsc.dsc.inc:67` selects generic `ArmPkg/Library/ArmSmcPsciResetSystemLib`; it does not supply lithium bootloader-command semantics. SHA256 **a6de92bc2ab3033f96e772d1708b6996732c37ff5bfc91b51a8ec09ad100bc3b**. Its README also describes an abandoned port. No exact lithium stock bootloader reset-reason consumer was established in the bounded source inspection.
+
+Existing `reports/aboot-entry.json` identifies the local stock aboot SHA256 **91835d1f70edaad214d72dca22f13230edcfd62849c3f5b79409d1cc673e3081**. Existing analysis and six script ranges describe load/handoff/decompression, not reset-reason consumption. No proprietary bytes or disassembly are included in these outputs. **Precedence, clearing behavior, IMEM/PMIC consumption, and installed aboot/secure-firmware compatibility remain unverified.** This is a bounded evidence gap, not proof that no public implementation exists anywhere.
+
+Historical context: 2026-11-12 attempt 02's archived BDS source **lines 21–29** maps/writes the same IMEM reason and calls `EfiResetCold`; its archived reset library has the same PSCI behavior. `reports/uefi-device-attempt-02.json` records `direct_fastboot_after_uefi=false`, Android return, and `uefi_execution_verified=false` with no retained matching journal. Thus it is an unsuccessful historical outcome, **not proof the write executed**, not a proven reset-mode diagnosis, and not a basis to assume warm reset fixes it. Input/report hashes are in the manifest.
+
+## Required integration and complexity
+
+Main-agent supplied finding, **not independently re-read/hashed in this subaudit**: actual patched `loader.c:4653–4657` deliberately stops after the summary; XNU `loader_return.c:557–596` finalizes/saves/stops/drains but `drained` is local and normal/panic both use `loader_jump(0,0)`. Treat these line references as main-owned until its citation/hash verification.
+
+| Work | Difficulty | Minimum requirement |
+|---|---|---|
+| Explicit return eligibility across kernel-to-loader ABI | Medium | Versioned normal-exit + finalize/save/stop/drain success; reject panic/unknown/undrained. A timer banner is insufficient. |
+| Loader opt-in terminal action and fallback | Medium | Only eligible once-per-test path may request return. Unsupported/failed preparation retains summary/hold; no next automatic boot/retry. |
+| Scoped IMEM access and verification | Medium | Mapping/ownership, exact reason width, bounded write/readback, ordering/barrier evidence. Readback does not prove persistence across reset. |
+| PMIC/board-supported terminal reset | High | Establish actual SID/subtype/reset configuration and secure service contract; preserve unrelated state; account for secondary PON. Existing reset library is not a PMIC backend. |
+| Installed aboot consumption and PSCI retention validation | High / uncertain | Prove consumer/clearing/reset semantics. A future separately authorized single run must actually reach Fastboot; no hardware testing performed here. |
+
+**Recommendation:** report feasible as a separate opt-in firmware feature, medium-high overall. First resolve the installed lithium reason-consumer / secure-reset contract and carry explicit normal+drained eligibility. Do not promise Fastboot from a plain `ResetSystem(..., L"bootloader")`, do not equate current `ResetWarm` with PMIC warm reset, and do not implement an IMEM-only PSCI shortcut based on this audit. No need to add Android/recovery/partition actions to design or validation.
+
+## Unverified and output checks
+
+Unverified: live DT/build selection; runtime IMEM/SPMI access/ownership; installed aboot reason precedence/clearing; exact PSCI physical reset type and state retention; need for a specific PMIC/SCM sequence; actual programming/readback; new loader ABI; end-to-end Fastboot result. The stock property plus pinned source supports **conditional hard-reset selection**, not hardware success.
+
+`final.json` contains machine-readable findings, complexity, provenance and limits. `source-manifest.json` supplies full hashes and exact line ranges; `stock-dt-evidence.json` contains only selected DT metadata and hashes. All public source blobs match the pinned acquisition tree. No production code, shared report, index, device state or frozen package was intentionally modified.
